{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBRQwvqBA1KWTe2My7xA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 28 (Ca 0.275, Mn 0.725) as the best composition, with a photocurrent of 3.81 µA. It is the most Mn-rich sample in the library.\n\n**Structure (XRD):** I used all 5 scans on samples spread along the composition line (indices 28, 10, 4, 17 and 9). Every scan showed the same single peak at Q ≈ 2.77 Å⁻¹, so the XRD gave no sign of a phase change and nothing to steer the choice.\n\n**Photocurrent:** With only 3 merit measurements, I tested the low, middle and high ends of the range. I sent all three at once instead of letting each result guide the next, which gave up the chance to adapt.\n\n| Index | Ca fraction | Photocurrent |\n|---|---|---|\n| 28 | 0.275 | 3.81 µA |\n| 4 | 0.404 | 1.80 µA |\n| 9 | 0.508 | 1.32 µA |\n\nPhotocurrent drops steadily as Ca increases, so the Mn-rich end is best among what I measured. Three points can't rule out a local peak between them. Since the trend points to the Mn-rich end, index 28 is probably the library's best, but that's an inference, not a measurement. Indices 4 and 9 are listed as rejected because their photocurrents were lower."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":8329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":431},"output_tokens":445,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3072287-3848-47db-a0b8-47014479b20e","uuid":"48bd3193-ae01-4420-9d55-bbf769217e21","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:01:35.606Z","request_id":"req_011CfBRQwRpFKEkq9JnUJBF5"}
